<title>USA: Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>Top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are ticket sales for the top movies at the U.S. box office over the Friday to Sunday weekend, according to estimates by Exhibitor Relations Co. Final data will be released on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Liar Liar ........................ $32.0 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Selena ........................... $11.0 million</p>
<p>    3 (1) Return of the Jedi ...............  $7.5 million</p>
<p>    4 (2) Jungle 2 Jungle ..................  $6.2 million</p>
<p>    5 (3) Private Parts ....................  $4.6 million</p>
<p>    6 (4) Donnie Brasco ....................  $3.5 million</p>
<p>    7 (7) Sling Blade ......................  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    8 (6) Love Jones .......................  $2.6 million</p>
<p>    9 (5) The Empire Strikes Back ..........  $2.5 million</p>
<p>   10(12) The English Patient ..............  $1.9 million</p>
<p>   10(13) Jerry Maguire ....................  $1.9 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures in parentheses are last week's rank.</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;Selena&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc.  &quot;Love Jones&quot; is released by Time Warner's New Line Cinema.</p>
<p>&quot;Return of the Jedi&quot; and &quot;The Empire Strikes Back&quot; are released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Jungle 2 Jungle&quot; is released by Walt Disney Co. while &quot;Sling Blade&quot; and &quot;The English Patient&quot; are released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Private Parts&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Donnie Brasco&quot; and &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; are released by Sony Corp.</p>
</text>
